      "documentConcept": "Crypto bot market-data freshness and stream integrity",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:238471e98222a5e0306517dcef44529ac5977467428af3b741059213c331c4d0",
      "text": "Market-data monitoring must check freshness per symbol and preserve exchange and receive times. Process heartbeats do not establish candle freshness. Snapshot-plus-stream order books require sequence-aware bootstrap and gap handling. Delivery guarantees differ by channel, and a recent candle update may still describe an unfinished candle. Silence can reflect an illiquid market as well as a failed stream, so freshness limits need context. REST fallback values should remain identifiable by source and timestamp. These checks establish whether the bot is consuming timely and coherent market data.",
